# Rules for LoanDepot React Project

## 1. Development Scope & AI Role

- **Developer Role (Full Logic & Architecture Responsibility)**:
  - You own 100% of the application architecture, component prop contracts, custom hooks, State/Redux Toolkit Query integration, React Hook Form, and event handlers.
- **Cursor Agent Role (Static UI/Layout Generator)**:
  - Generate ONLY static JSX structures and Tailwind CSS v4 styling based on Figma screenshots and tasks.
  - DO NOT write component props, event handlers, useState/useReducer hooks, or API fetching logic.
  - Output raw, hardcoded static markup so the developer can independently refactor it into clean, parametrised components.

## 2. Design System & Color Palette

- **ALLOWED COLORS ONLY**: You MUST ONLY use the custom Tailwind brand colors defined in `@theme` inside `src/index.css`. NEVER use default Tailwind color numbers or raw HEX values:
  - `bg-brand-purple-dark`, `text-brand-purple-dark` (#301A37)
  - `bg-brand-purple`, `text-brand-purple`, `border-brand-purple` (#6D53AF)
  - `bg-brand-green`, `text-brand-green`, `border-brand-green` (#9EC73D)
  - `bg-brand-green-alt` (#A9CA5B)
  - `bg-brand-gray`, `text-brand-gray`, `border-brand-gray` (#979797)
  - `bg-brand-gray-light`, `border-brand-gray-light` (#E2E2E2)
  - `bg-brand-light`, `text-brand-light` (#FAFAFA)
  - Standard pure black/white (`bg-black`, `text-white`) when explicitly needed.

## 3. Project Documentation & Specifications

- Primary requirements and section breakdowns reside in `docs/Task.md`.
- Component hierarchy and layout boundaries are documented in `docs/architecture.md`.

## 4. Code Quality & Standards

- Mobile-first responsive layout (desktop sections set to `h-screen` / `100vh`).
- All generated code must pass Oxlint without warnings or syntax issues.
